    /// [Unix Time Stamp](https://www.unixtimestamp.com/) of the change. Past changes (new,
    /// updated, removed) will always have a timestamp. Future changes (expiring, upcoming) will
    /// have a timestamp if the exact date is known. If not, timestamp will be omitted, e.g. a
    /// show is known to be expiring soon, but the exact date is not known.
